2025-05-20 23:21:00,"{""skill"": ""Function of Sentence"", ""difficulty"": ""Easy"", ""question"": ""During World War II, countless women stepped outside the domestic sphere to work in factories, offices, and other roles previously dominated by men. _They filled vital positions in manufacturing, production, and administration, ensuring that factories continued to supply troops with necessary resources even as men fought on the front lines._ Encouraged by government campaigns, women learned new skills, took on new responsibilities, and in many cases, helped run entire operations. This transformation not only contributed to the war effort but also laid the foundation for changing perceptions of women’s capabilities in the workforce.\n\nWhich choice best describes the function of the underlined sentence in the context of the paragraph?"", ""choices"": [""A. To present a counterexample to the notion that women’s roles remained strictly domestic"", ""B. To show how women’s involvement in the workforce replaced government-run initiatives"", ""C. To illustrate the essential role that women played in ensuring continuous production during the war"", ""D. To provide historical evidence that women were hesitant to participate in wartime labor""], ""answer"": ""C"", ""explanation"": ""Choice C is correct because the underlined sentence demonstrates how women took on important jobs in factories and administration, keeping vital production lines running while men were away fighting in the war. This focus on their core contribution clearly serves to highlight their integral role and confirms their significant impact. Choices A and B do not align with how the sentence shows women’s active work to maintain production lines. Choice D is incorrect because the sentence does not indicate any hesitancy; instead, it shows women willingly fulfilling essential duties."", ""topic"": ""The role of women in the workforce during World War II""}",Function of Sentence,Easy,"During World War II, c