2025-05-20 23:22:01,"{""skill"": ""Function of Sentence"", ""difficulty"": ""Easy"", ""question"": ""Social proof is a powerful concept in marketing, describing how people often rely on the opinions and actions of others to guide their own decisions. Many campaigns showcase online ratings, peer reviews, or celebrity endorsements to demonstrate a product’s popularity. _Marketers realize that endorsements from experts or well-known authorities can have an even greater impact on an audience’s perception of a brand._ This heightened trust in authoritative figures helps to reinforce the belief that the product is of high quality.\n\nWhich choice best describes the function of the underlined sentence in the text as a whole?"", ""choices"": [""A) It hints that marketers prefer ignoring customer feedback in favor of expert endorsements."", ""B) It presents an example of a success story in which a product gained popularity due to social media influencers."", ""C) It describes how marketers must always rely on celebrity endorsements for any successful campaign."", ""D) It highlights why consumers may find endorsements from recognized professionals more credible.""], ""answer"": ""D"", ""explanation"": ""Choice D is correct because the underlined sentence emphasizes the added credibility consumers grant to a product when it is backed by an expert or recognized authority. The text initially introduces social proof, and then the underlined statement specifies that endorsements from credible figures can amplify this effect. The other choices either misrepresent the overall claim or place an incorrect emphasis on the role of experts and endorsements."", ""topic"": ""The concept of social proof in marketing and influence""}",Function of Sentence,Easy,"Social proof is a powerful concept in marketing, describing how people often rely on the opinions and actions of others to guide their own decisions. Many campaigns showcase online ratings, peer reviews, or celebrity endorsements to d