2025-05-20 23:23:11,"{""skill"": ""Function of Sentence"", ""difficulty"": ""Medium"", ""question"": ""Recent research indicates that prions—misfolded proteins—can trigger fatal neurodegenerative diseases by converting healthy proteins into abnormal forms. These misfolded proteins pile up in the brain, damaging neurons and leading to conditions such as Creutzfeldt–Jakob disease.\n\n_By forming large aggregates that tangibly disrupt normal neuronal activity, prions severely impair brain function._\n\nBecause prions resist common decontamination methods, they represent a significant challenge for biomedical research and public health, forcing scientists to develop more rigorous laboratory protocols.\n\nWhich choice best describes the function of the underlined sentence in the text as a whole?"", ""choices"": [""A. It acknowledges that prions can be neutralized if properly sterilized."", ""B. It illustrates the specific toxic effect prions have on brain cells, supporting the idea that prions play a direct role in causing neurodegeneration."", ""C. It highlights a historical context for prion discovery, contradicting an earlier claim in the text."", ""D. It provides evidence that prions, unlike most proteins, do not rely on host cells for replication.""], ""answer"": ""B"", ""explanation"": ""Choice B is correct because the underlined sentence shows exactly how prion aggregates interfere with normal neurological function: they disrupt neuronal activity so severely that the resulting damage contributes to serious neurodegeneration. The rest of the paragraph describes prions’ resistance to decontamination and the difficulties they pose for research and public health. Thus, the underlined portion underscores prions’ role in harming neurons. A is incorrect because the sentence does not discuss techniques for neutralizing prions. C is incorrect because it does not offer historical context that contradicts any claim. D is incorrect because the sentence does not address prion replication methods but instead focuses on how aggregates impair neurons."", ""topic"": ""The role of prions in neurodegenerative diseases""}",Function of Sentence,Medium,"Recent research indicates that prions—misfolded proteins—can trigger fatal neurodegenerative diseases by converting healthy proteins into abnormal forms. These misfolded proteins pile up in the brain, damaging neurons and leading to conditions such as Creutzfeldt–Jakob disease.

