rained biases, thus setting up a defense that endorses the transformation advocated by feminists. Although the other choices might reflect aspects of the broader debate, none captures how the underlined sentence specifically serves as a critique that the text subsequently addresses. Its primary function is to underscore a major concern critics have about feminist approaches, which the ensuing text rebuts."", ""topic"": ""The role of feminism in contemporary political philosophy""}",Function of Sentence,Hard,"Many contemporary political theorists contend that feminist perspectives have reshaped normative frameworks by pushing for greater inclusivity and intersectionality in the analysis of power dynamics. They emphasize the necessity of recognizing how gender, race, and class converge to influence policy outcomes, thereby expanding the scope of debates around freedom and equality. _Critics claim that these scholarly calls for fundamental structural reform ignore feasible, incremental policy action and thus undermine consensus building among legislators._ Still, advocates of feminist approaches maintain that politics must prioritize dismantling entrenched biases, even at the risk of engendering short-term disagreement, to achieve genuine societal transformation.

