2025-05-20 23:31:51,"{""skill"": ""Inferences"", ""difficulty"": ""Easy"", ""question"": ""During the early 1770s, tensions rose among the American colonists when the British Parliament passed the Tea Act to raise revenue. Many colonists viewed these taxes as unjust, arguing that they had no representation in Parliament. In December 1773, a group of colonists boarded ships in Boston Harbor and dumped hundreds of tea chests into the water, an event that became known as the Boston Tea Party. Soon after, Parliament passed the Coercive Acts, which only increased colonial anger and helped set the stage for the American Revolution.\n\nWhich statement can most reasonably be inferred from the passage?"", ""choices"": [""A. The British government’s strict reaction to the Boston Tea Party worsened tensions with the colonies."", ""B. Colonists immediately decided to end all taxes on British tea by electing their own representatives."", ""C. The Coercive Acts prompted colonists to quickly pay the taxes on tea to avoid more conflict."", ""D. The Boston Tea Party convinced Parliament to stop enforcing taxes in all the American colonies.""], ""answer"": ""A"", ""explanation"": ""Choice A is correct because the passage describes how Parliament responded with harsh policies (the Coercive Acts), which further angered the colonists and led to increased tension. This suggests that the government’s severe reaction ultimately worsened the situation. Choices B, C, and D are not supported by the passage because there is no evidence that colonists immediately ended taxes, aimed to pay taxes, or convinced Parliament to halt taxation. Instead, the passage emphasizes that stricter UK policies raised tensions even higher."", ""topic"": ""The causes and effects of the Boston Tea Party""}",Inferences,Easy,"During the early 1770s, tensions rose among the American colonists when the British Parliament passed the Tea Act to raise revenue. Many colonists viewed these taxes as unjust, arguing that they had no representation in Parliament. In December 1773, a group of colonists boarded ships in Boston Harbor and dumped hundreds of tea chests into the water, an event that became known as the Boston Tea Party. Soon after, Parliament passed the Coercive Acts, which only increased colonial anger and helped set the stage for the American Revolution.

