ewpoint, that they are primarily concerned about content accuracy, or that they are generally unaware of an article’s influence."", ""topic"": ""The role of cognitive biases in shaping political opinions""}","Researchers examined a group of people who read online news articles that reinforced their existing political views. The participants shared these articles widely on social media and rarely explored alternative viewpoints, suggesting they favored content that agreed with their initial opinions.

