2025-05-20 23:48:06,"{""skill"": ""Inferences"", ""difficulty"": ""Hard"", ""question"": ""Developers of an advanced artificial intelligence platform designed to screen job applicants have found that the algorithm's decisions occasionally perpetuate biased outcomes, even when historical data is removed and the AI is given new training examples. The platform relies on sophisticated pattern-recognition techniques that incorporate subtle correlations from older datasets and reintroduce them into each new model. Several researchers argue that while ensuring fairness requires limiting potentially prejudicial factors (like socioeconomic background), the AI itself may still infer other unintentional proxies that are ethically questionable. However, some developers maintain that more extensive oversight and transparency measures can mitigate these risks without sacrificing the efficiency of automated decisions.\n\nWhich conclusion is best supported by the information in the text?"", ""choices"": [""A. Eliminating all links to previous training data guarantees that the AI outputs will be completely free of bias."", ""B. Oversight and transparency measures cannot fully rectify biases if the AI continues to identify hidden correlations."", ""C. Restricting a single demographic factor ensures that most discriminatory patterns will be eliminated immediately."", ""D. Adjusting the data to reflect only recent societal shifts makes oversight unnecessary for ethical screening.""], ""answer"": ""B"", ""explanation"": ""The text states that although removing historical data can reduce certain forms of bias, the AI may still learn similarly biased patterns through hidden correlations. Researchers suggest that even with deliberate safeguards, the method by which the AI seeks new proxies remains an ethical concern. Therefore, oversight and transparency alone are not sufficient to prevent the AI from detecting other angles that introduce unfairness. Answer A is incorrect because removing 