2025-05-20 23:53:59,"{""skill"": ""Main Idea"", ""difficulty"": ""Easy"", ""question"": ""The following text is from a historical overview of the Persian Empire’s influence on commerce in the ancient world.\n\nBeginning around 550 BCE, the Persian Empire solidified its position as an economic bridge between regions in Asia and the Mediterranean. Although its primary goal was to extend governance and maintain authority, the empire’s rulers built and maintained roads that spanned great distances, aiding the transport of goods and resources across their vast territory. Merchants were able to exchange luxury items, metals, and agricultural products, which not only enriched the empire but also promoted cultural ties with neighboring civilizations.\n\nWhich choice best states the main idea of the text?"", ""choices"": [""A. The Persian Empire’s road network helped promote trade and cultural links among distant regions."", ""B. The Persian Empire strived to limit the flow of goods in order to protect its resources."", ""C. Most trade in the empire focused solely on agricultural products from remote areas."", ""D. Luxury items brought into the empire were more important than any other type of resource.""], ""answer"": ""A"", ""explanation"": ""Choice A is correct because the passage clearly shows how Persia’s extensive road system made it easier to transport goods, enriching the empire and fostering connections between different cultures. The text describes how trade in luxury items, metals, and agricultural products flourished and influenced regions beyond Persia. The other options focus on limiting trade or suggesting that only certain goods were traded, which does not match the idea presented in the passage."", ""topic"": ""The role of the Persian Empire in shaping early global trade""}",Main Idea,Easy,"The following text is from a historical overview of the Persian Empire’s influence on commerce in the ancient world.

