2025-05-20 23:55:06,"{""skill"": ""Main Idea"", ""difficulty"": ""Easy"", ""question"": ""The following text is adapted from \""Observations on Subtle Language\"".\n\nIn her sociology paper, Kayla describes how subtle remarks can reveal unconscious biases. She focuses on microaggressions, short statements or actions that unintentionally convey prejudice. Microaggressions can be small insults or behavioral slights people show toward someone based on their identity. Kayla argues that while these gestures may appear trivial, they often create an uncomfortable environment over time. This discomfort can hinder open conversations and reinforce unfavorable stereotypes during everyday encounters.\n\nWhich choice best states the main idea of the text?"", ""choices"": [""A. They highlight how unintentional remarks can negatively influence everyday interactions."", ""B. They show how microaggressions have only recently emerged as a social phenomenon."", ""C. They examine why people must always avoid any type of personal interaction."", ""D. They describe how overt discrimination is more serious than subtle forms.""], ""answer"": ""A"", ""explanation"": ""Choice A is correct because the passage describes how microaggressions, even if subtle or unintentional, can create discomfort and reinforce prejudices in everyday interactions. These negative effects highlight how small acts can have a larger impact on people’s social experiences. Choice B is incorrect because the text doesn’t claim that microaggressions are newly identified. Choice C is incorrect because the text doesn’t suggest that people should avoid interaction. Choice D is incorrect because the text doesn’t make a direct comparison between overt discrimination and subtle slights, focusing instead on the consequences of subtle negative remarks."", ""topic"": ""How microaggressions shape everyday interactions""}",Main Idea,Easy,"The following text is adapted from ""Observations on Subtle Language"".

In her sociology paper, Kayla describes how subtle remarks can reveal unconscious biases. She focuses on microaggressions, short statements or actions that unintentionally convey prejudice. Microaggressions can be small insults or behavioral slights people show toward someone based on their identity. Kayla argues that while these gestures may appear trivial, they often create an uncomfortable environment over time. This discomfort can hinder open conversations and reinforce unfavorable stereotypes during everyday encounters.

Which choice best states the main idea of the text?","A. They highlight how unintentional remarks can negatively influence everyday interactions.
