2025-05-20 23:56:19,"{""skill"": ""Main Idea"", ""difficulty"": ""Easy"", ""question"": ""The following text is an introduction to absolute zero, the lowest temperature theoretically possible.\n\nPhysicists define absolute zero, or 0 Kelvin, as the point at which the particles of any substance have the least possible amount of thermal energy. Though scientists cannot reach this temperature exactly, recent advancements in cooling methods let researchers come extremely close. At these ultralow temperatures, matter can exhibit unusual quantum behaviors, providing key insights into the fundamental nature of particles while also driving developments in fields such as superconductivity and quantum computing.\n\nWhich choice best states the main idea of the text?"", ""choices"": [""A. Absolute zero can be easily achieved using ordinary cooling equipment."", ""B. Studying extremely low temperatures helps physicists deepen their understanding of matter and discover new phenomena."", ""C. Reaching absolute zero is a simple process that always results in superconductivity."", ""D. Particles move faster at lower temperatures, contrasting previous theories about absolute zero.""], ""answer"": ""B"", ""explanation"": ""The text emphasizes that absolute zero cannot be perfectly attained but that research near ultralow temperatures leads physicists toward new discoveries about particle behavior and important advances in fields like superconductivity and quantum computing. Thus, the passage’s main idea is that scientists’ exploration of near-absolute-zero conditions yields deeper knowledge and novel phenomena. Other choices either suggest it is easy to reach absolute zero or misrepresent the nature of particle motion at low temperatures."", ""topic"": ""The concept of absolute zero and its implications for physics""}",Main Idea,Easy,"The following text is an introduction to absolute zero, the lowest temperature theoretically possible.

Physicists define absolute zero, or 0 Kelvin, as the point at which the particles of any substance have the least possible amount of thermal energy. Though scientists cannot reach this temperature exactly, recent advancements in cooling methods let researchers come extremely close. At these ultralow temperatures, matter can exhibit unusual quantum behaviors, providing key insights into the fundamental nature of particles while also driving developments in fields such as superconductivity and quantum computing.

Which choice best states the main idea of the text?","A. Absolute zero can be easily achieved using ordinary cooling equipment.
B. Studying extremely low temperatures helps physicists deepen their understanding of matter and discover new phenomena.
C. Reaching absolute zero is a simple process that always results in superconductivity.
