2025-05-20 23:59:32,"{""skill"": ""Main Idea"", ""difficulty"": ""Medium"", ""question"": ""The following text is excerpted from a 2021 essay discussing how postmodern perspectives have reshaped modern political and ethical debates. Postmodernism, with its skepticism toward universal truth, has prompted individuals to question once-dominant narratives and reevaluate traditional moral frameworks. Some observers believe that this shift encourages more diverse perspectives in political conversations, promoting open exchange. Others warn that a strong emphasis on subjectivity can reduce confidence in shared norms, potentially causing public discourse to fragment and making it harder to reach consensus.\n\nWhich choice best states the main idea of the text?\n\nA) Postmodern skepticism has led many to assert the existence of absolute moral truths.\nB) Highlighting divergent opinions seldom results in productive public debates.\nC) Emphasizing subjectivity can broaden political and ethical dialogue but complicate agreement.\nD) Postmodern thought views all moral standards as invalid and indefensible."", ""choices"": [""A) Postmodern skepticism has led many to assert the existence of absolute moral truths."", ""B) Highlighting divergent opinions seldom results in productive public debates."", ""C) Emphasizing subjectivity can broaden political and ethical dialogue but complicate agreement."", ""D) Postmodern thought views all moral standards as invalid and indefensible.""], ""answer"": ""C"", ""explanation"": ""Choice C is correct because the text describes how postmodernism questions absolute truths and encourages multiple viewpoints, potentially making it harder to form a shared consensus. This suggests that while subjectivity can expand discourse, it may also undermine agreement. Choice A is incorrect because the text indicates that postmodernism is suspicious of absolute truths rather than supportive of them. Choice B is inaccurate, as the text suggests that welcoming m