k"": ""The question is appropriately labeled as Medium difficulty. The passage length (roughly 100 words including the introductory sentence) and the need to synthesize the idea of political engagement from multiple sentences align well with the SAT medium-level expectations. To further align with Medium difficulty, you might consider adjusting one or two distractors to be slightly more nuanced, thereby increasing the challenge for students aiming for a 600–700 SAT score.""}"
2025-05-21 00:02:01,"{""skill"": ""Main Idea"", ""difficulty"": ""Medium"", ""question"": ""In the early 20th century, Spanish artist Pablo Picasso shattered conventions by experimenting with perspective, form, and color. Co-creating Cubism with Georges Braque, Picasso explored multiple viewpoints within a single composition, challenging the long-established rules of representation. He also frequently shifted styles, moving from his emotionally charged Blue Period to phases that drew on African art for inspiration, spurring new creative avenues in painting and sculpture. Yet the core of his work remained focused on pushing boundaries, encouraging the emergence of innovative movements that shaped the ideals and techniques of modern art.\n\nWhich choice best states the main idea of the text?"", ""choices"": [""A) Picasso maintained a consistent approach throughout his career and influenced a small circle of modern artists."", ""B) Picasso’s stylistic experimentation and break with tradition laid important groundwork for the development of modern art."", ""C) Picasso’s focus on realistic portrayals of subjects limited the range of modern artistic styles that followed."", ""D) Picasso’s interest in African art overshadowed other aspects of his contribution to modern art movements.""], ""answer"": ""B"", ""explanation"": ""The passage emphasizes how Picasso’s drive to challenge established norms and experiment with various styles helped shape and encourage modern art. Choice B captures this central theme by describing how Picasso’s boundary-pushing methods influenced new artistic directions. In contrast, choice A incorrectly suggests Picasso had a consistent approach. Choice C is contradicted by the text, which makes clear that Picasso’s art was far from strictly realistic. Choice D overstates Picasso’s engagement with African art, ignoring his broad impact across multiple styles and techniques."", ""topic"": ""The impact of Pablo Picasso on modern art""}",Main Idea,Medi