2025-05-21 00:42:06,"{""skill"": ""Punctuation"", ""difficulty"": ""Easy"", ""question"": ""Margaret Thatcher served as Britain’s prime minister from 1979 to 1990 and led the Conservative Party with a strong emphasis on reducing government intervention in the economy. Her firm approach to leadership earned her the nickname “Iron Lady.”\n\nWhich choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?\n\nMargaret Thatcher served as the Conservative Party leader ________ she was known for her unwavering stance on free-market reforms."", ""choices"": [""A) leader but she was"", ""B) leader and, she was"", ""C) leader; she was"", ""D) leader, and she was""], ""answer"": ""D"", ""explanation"": ""Choice D is the best answer because it uses a comma and a coordinating conjunction (and) to join two independent clauses properly. “Margaret Thatcher served as the Conservative Party leader” is an independent clause, and “she was known for her unwavering stance on free-market reforms” is another. When two clauses are both complete thoughts, they should be separated by a comma and a conjunction. The other choices either omit the necessary comma, add punctuation in the wrong place, or use a semicolon incorrectly in this context."", ""topic"": ""The political leadership of Margaret Thatcher in Britain""}",Punctuation,Easy,"Margaret Thatcher served as Britain’s prime minister from 1979 to 1990 and led the Conservative Party with a strong emphasis on reducing government intervention in the economy. Her firm approach to leadership earned her the nickname “Iron Lady.”

Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?

