2025-05-21 01:32:28,"{""skill"": ""Supporting Claims"", ""difficulty"": ""Easy"", ""question"": ""Researchers studying advanced neural networks have proposed that training these models on vast and varied datasets can help them adapt to many new tasks, such as recognizing handwritten characters or identifying subtle features in images. As the data volume and diversity increase, the network learns to generalize by observing many different examples, potentially performing well on challenges it has never faced before.\n\nWhich statement from the researchers’ summary best supports the claim that neural networks can learn to handle new tasks by analyzing large and varied datasets?"", ""choices"": [""A. A model trained on half a million images was later able to identify objects it had never encountered in training with remarkable accuracy."", ""B. One researcher commented that older software libraries need updating before the model can recognize handwritten notes accurately."", ""C. The summary emphasizes that even small-scale networks can make significant contributions when used alongside manual input."", ""D. Some experts highlight that hardware upgrades alone guarantee only limited performance gains across different learning tasks.""], ""answer"": ""A"", ""explanation"": ""Choice A clearly shows that training with a large dataset allowed the neural network to identify unfamiliar objects, directly supporting the claim that increased data variety and quantity helps these systems adapt to new problems. By contrast, the other statements focus either on technical software updates, on smaller networks, or on hardware considerations rather than on demonstrating how extensive training data enables the network to learn and generalize more effectively."", ""topic"": ""The development of artificial intelligence and neural networks""}",Supporting Claims,Easy,"Researchers studying advanced neural networks have proposed that training these models on vast and varied datasets can help 