2025-05-21 01:33:40,"{""skill"": ""Supporting Claims"", ""difficulty"": ""Easy"", ""question"": ""Many economists note that adopting climate change policies typically requires businesses to make upfront investments, such as purchasing energy-efficient machinery or switching to cleaner energy sources. However, supporters argue that these costs can be offset in the long run through lower utility bills, reduced waste, and potential government incentives.\n\nWhich statement from a local business owner best supports the claim that climate change policies can reduce costs over time for businesses?"", ""choices"": [""A) Our main concern was how to manage a new marketing campaign for our eco-friendly products, but we haven’t developed one yet."", ""B) We found an innovative solar panel system at a good price, though it still needs regular maintenance."", ""C) We considered investing in electric vehicles for our company fleet, but we decided to focus on traditional cars for now."", ""D) By installing insulated windows and upgrading our lighting system, we’ve cut our monthly energy costs by nearly 30%.""], ""answer"": ""D"", ""explanation"": ""Choice D specifically shows the company achieving a measurable decrease in energy costs after making investments that align with climate change policies. This direct evidence supports the idea that such policies can lead to long-term savings. The other choices do not clearly demonstrate reduced expenses. They either describe future plans, mention maintenance without noting any cost savings, or indicate no pursuit of climate-friendly options."", ""topic"": ""The economic implications of climate change policies""}",Supporting Claims,Easy,"Many economists note that adopting climate change policies typically requires businesses to make upfront investments, such as purchasing energy-efficient machinery or switching to cleaner energy sources. However, supporters argue that these costs can be offset in the long run through lower utility bills,