2025-05-21 01:52:39,"{""skill"": ""Synthesizing Notes"", ""difficulty"": ""Easy"", ""question"": ""While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:\n\n• Status anxiety arises when individuals worry about how others judge their social and economic standing.\n\n• In modern consumer culture, people often buy luxury or brand-name goods to appear more successful.\n\n• Social media can intensify comparisons and heighten status anxiety among users.\n\n• Many individuals overspend or go into debt because they believe it will help them project a higher social status.\n\n\nThe student wants to emphasize how status anxiety influences the purchasing decisions of consumers.\n\nWhich choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?"", ""choices"": [""A. Social media can intensify comparisons among consumers who buy luxury goods and overspend."", ""B. Buyers often feel pressured by status anxiety to purchase high-end products, even if it means spending beyond their means to seem more successful."", ""C. Status anxiety generally causes people to avoid social media so that they do not have to compare their possessions with others."", ""D. Many consumers are concerned about social judgment on social media, but they seldom purchase brand-name items.""], ""answer"": ""B"", ""explanation"": ""Choice B succinctly connects the notes about overspending to appear more successful, highlighting how status anxiety can drive such behavior. Choices A and D focus on social media or brand names without clearly stating how status anxiety leads to those purchases. Choice C inaccurately claims status anxiety causes people to avoid social media rather than engage in overspending."", ""topic"": ""The role of status anxiety in modern consumer culture""}",Synthesizing Notes,Easy,"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:

