2025-05-21 01:56:18,"{""skill"": ""Synthesizing Notes"", ""difficulty"": ""Easy"", ""question"": ""While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:\n\n• Transhumanism is an approach that uses technology to enhance human capabilities beyond normal limits.\n\n• Proponents believe genetically engineering humans could reduce diseases and extend healthy lifespans.\n\n• Critics say human enhancement could worsen inequality if only certain groups can afford these technologies.\n\n• Some worry that enhancing human abilities might raise questions about the value of natural human limits.\n\nThe student wants to highlight a key concern about human enhancement. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?\n\n"", ""choices"": [""A. Critics note that if only certain groups could afford enhancements, transhumanist technologies could worsen inequality among people."", ""B. Some people suggest that genetic engineering might eliminate diseases, allowing everyone to enjoy better health."", ""C. Transhumanism is about going beyond human limits by using biotechnology to prolong life and improve health."", ""D. Many experts believe the best benefit of transhumanism is that it completely removes all moral worries about altering human nature.""], ""answer"": ""A"", ""explanation"": ""Choice A best emphasizes the concern that human enhancements could spark inequality, which matches the notes about affordability and social fairness. Choice B focuses on potential benefits rather than highlighting a key concern. Choice C simply describes the goal of transhumanism without addressing a worry about it. Choice D claims that transhumanism removes moral concerns, which is contradictory to the notes mentioning questions about natural human limits and inequality."", ""topic"": ""The ethical implications of transhumanism and human enhancement""}",Synthesizing Notes,Easy,"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following no