2025-05-21 01:57:29,"{""skill"": ""Synthesizing Notes"", ""difficulty"": ""Easy"", ""question"": ""While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:\n\n• During the late 19th and early 20th centuries, feminist activists challenged restrictive clothing, such as corsets, by promoting simpler, less confining garments.\n\n• Greater acceptance of shorter hemlines reflected changing attitudes toward women’s independence and self-expression.\n\n• Some observers linked shifts in clothing choices to the broader goals of equal rights.\n\nThe student wants to highlight how the feminist movement promoted more practical, less confining clothing options for women. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?\n\n"", ""choices"": [""A. During the late 19th century, many feminists chose to wear corsets in public to demonstrate their independence."", ""B. As activists pursued their broader goals of equal rights, they mainly emphasized the importance of voting rather than fashion trends."", ""C. Some observers suggested that simpler styles were connected to women’s growing social and political influence."", ""D. Because feminist activists supported shorter hemlines and simpler designs, many women abandoned corsets for more practical forms of clothing.""], ""answer"": ""D"", ""explanation"": ""Choice D is the best answer because it directly connects the ideas in the notes: that feminist activists challenged restrictive garments like corsets and encouraged simpler options, including shorter hemlines. Choices A, B, and C each omit or misrepresent important details about the move away from restrictive clothing, failing to accomplish the goal of highlighting how the feminist movement promoted more practical clothing options."", ""topic"": ""The impact of the feminist movement on fashion trends""}",Synthesizing Notes,Easy,"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:

