ng forms of bias and their impact on those with overlapping identities. This aligns with the student's goal of clarifying the concept for an audience familiar with basic discrimination but not its compounded effects. Choices A and B misrepresent the idea of interaction among biases, while choice D inaccurately narrows the scope of intersectionality to specific forms of bias."", ""topic"": ""How intersectionality shapes experiences of discrimination"", ""total_score"": 27, ""constructive_feedback"": ""The question is well-constructed and clearly aligned with SAT guidelines for synthesizing information from notes. The bullet points provide sufficient detail and the objective is specific enough to target a basic definition of intersectionality. The answer choices include plausible distractors that force students to differentiate between the accurate synthesis and common misinterpretations. For improvement, ensure the bullet formatting strictly follows the \n\n• format as required, and consider slightly refining the objective wording to emphasize the overlapping nature of discrimination. Adding another subtle trap among the distractors could further challenge students without compromising clarity."", ""difficulty_feedback"": ""The question fits medium-difficulty expectations by requiring multi-step reasoning, careful selection of relevant details, and synthesis of a clear definition. The length of the question is within the acceptable range, and the distractor choices are moderately challenging. To further heighten the challenge, consider lengthening the notes very slightly or incorporating another distractor that represents a nearly correct but subtly flawed interpretation.""}"
2025-05-21 02:05:20,"{""skill"": ""Synthesizing Notes"", ""difficulty"": ""Medium"", ""question"": ""While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:\n\n• Marine organisms sometimes ingest plastic debris, which can block their digestive tracts.\n\n• Fragments known as microplastics have spread throughout ocean regions, even remote ones.\n\n• According to Dr. Faulkner’s study, microplastics have been found in the tissues of fish in coastal areas.\n\n• Plastic pollution exposes aquatic species to toxins that may disrupt their reproductive systems.\n\nThe student wants to highlight Dr. Faulkner’s research findings to an audience unfamiliar with the effects of plastic pollution on marine life.\n\nWhich choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?"", ""choices"": [""A. Dr. Faulkner explained that marine organisms sometimes ingest plastic debris that can block digestion and expose them to toxins."", ""B. Plastic debris has proliferated worldwide, affecting the reproductive systems of many fish in remote regions of the ocean."", ""C. According to Dr. Faulkner, fragments known as microplastics have been found in fish tissues, demonstrating how plastic pollution can disrupt marine life."", ""D. Microplastics occur in a variety of ocean habitats, so fish and other aquatic species can ingest them and may face serious health risks.""], ""answer"": ""C"", ""explanation"": ""Choice C is the best answer because it cites Dr. Faulkner’s finding—that microplastics were discovered in the tissues of fish in coastal areas—and links it to the broader threat plastic debris poses to marine organisms. This direct connection addresses the student’s goal of highlighting Dr. Faulkner’s research findings to an audience not yet aware of how plastic pollution can affect marine life. Choice A is incorrect because it focuses on general effects of plastic debris but does not specifically highlight Dr. Faulkner’s findings. Choice B is incorrect because it overstates the geographical spread of reproductive effects without referencing the study. Choice D is too broad, mentioning possible health risks but lacking explicit mention of Dr. Faulkner’s findings."", ""topic"": ""The impact of plastic pollution on marine life""}",Synthesizing Notes,Medium,"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:

