• formatting and consider slightly enriching the vocabulary or adding an extra detail to bring the passage squarely within the 120–150 word target. Overall, this question is nearly publication-ready.",9,27,"{""skill"": ""Synthesizing Notes"", ""difficulty"": ""Hard"", ""question"": ""While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:\n\n• A 2021 study by the Urban Institute found that sprawling metropolitan areas frequently experience tighter housing markets, leading to surging rent prices that disproportionately impact low-income families.\n• The study highlighted how inadequate public transportation in suburban enclaves limits job opportunities for lower-wage earners.\n• It detailed significant inequities in funding for vital services like education, resulting in reduced social mobility for underprivileged populations.\n• The study also noted that affluent households moving to suburban areas deprive city centers of tax revenue, which exacerbates economic disparities.\n\nThe student wants to highlight how these interrelated issues deepen socioeconomic inequity and advocate for policy solutions addressing both housing affordability and transportation accessibility. Which choice most effectively synthesizes relevant information from these notes to fulfill this objective?"", ""choices"": [""A. In sprawling regions, transportation limitations and high rent hinder mobility, yet not all experts concur on suburbanization's role in rising living costs."", ""B. Funding inequities in suburban schools can marginally impact mobility, but they do not directly connect to limited job opportunities for working-class residents."", ""C. Studies reveal that rising rents, insufficient transit systems, and funding disparities in education collectively perpetuate socioeconomic divides, underscoring the need for policies promoting both affordable housing and improved mobility."", ""D. While some claim tax bases decline in city centers due to suburban growth, others assert that economic opportunities abound within suburban expansion projects.""], ""answer"": ""C"", ""explanation"": ""Choice C effectively summarizes the interplay among housing, transportation, and education inequities in worsening socioeconomic divides. It also supports the student's focus on policy advocacy for housing and transportation improvements. Choice A downplays the role of suburbanization in rising rents, choice B inadequately connects funding issues to employment accessibility, and choice D incorrectly emphasizes the benefits of suburban growth without acknowledging the related inequalities."", ""topic"": ""The effects of urban sprawl on social and economic inequality"", ""total_score"": 27, ""constructive_feedback"": ""The question is well-constructed and clearly aligned with the SAT's hard difficulty standards. It provides a sufficiently detailed set of bullet-point notes and a clear objective, requiring students to synthesize multiple pieces of information. The answer choices are sophisticated and include subtle traps that test in-depth reasoning. The explanation is concise and effectively justifies why choice C is correct while critiquing the distractors. To further improve, ensure that the bullet points strictly use the designated \n\n• formatting and consider slightly enriching the vocabulary or adding an extra detail to bring the passage squarely within the 120–150 word target. Overall, this question is nearly publication-ready."", ""difficulty_feedback"": ""This question appropriately matches its labeled hard difficulty. It employs complex language, multi-step reasoning, and nuanced distractors that challenge even high-performing students. A minor tweak to length or enrichment of some details could further tighten its alignment with the hard criteria, but overall it excellently meets the intended complexity.""}"
2025-05-21 02:19:23,"{""skill"": ""Synthesizing Notes"", ""difficulty"": ""Hard"", ""question"": ""While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes from the 2023 White Paper by the Global Energy Institute:\n\n• The International Energy Agency forecasts that global demand for renewable electricity will grow by over 40% within the next five years.\n\n• The largest projected increases in energy storage capacity are linked to improvements in lithium-ion battery manufacturing.\n\n• Some researchers now explore solid-state battery designs, which they believe can achieve higher energy densities and reduce charging times.\n\n• Analysts suggest that better battery recycling infrastructure could offset concerns around raw materials like lithium and cobalt.\n\n• A pilot solar farm in the southwestern United States reported notable energy surpluses after pairing photovoltaic panels with a second-generation battery storage system.\n\n• The White Paper warns of continued reliance on fossil fuels in regions lacking robust charging infrastructure or favorable policy incentives.\n\nThe student wants to craft a concluding statement that acknowledges the promising breakthroughs in both current and next-generation batteries while emphasizing the hurdles posed by reliance on fossil fuels and insufficient infrastructure in certain areas. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?"", ""choices"": [""A. Although many regions will continue to depend on fossil fuels, the International Energy Agency anticipates that renewable electricity will still grow by nearly half over the next five years."", ""B. Encouraging energy recycling programs is vital for minimizing the environmental impact in areas that do not have reliable charging stations or emerging technologies such as solid-state cells."", ""C. The southwestern United States demonstrates how integrated renewable systems can replace conventional fuels, as seen by the pilot solar farm’s reported surpluses from a second-generation battery system."", ""D. Even as global renewable electricity demand is poised for significant expansion and new battery designs are emerging, reliance on fossil fuels in regions with limited infrastructure remains a critical challenge.""], ""answer"": ""D"", ""explanation"": ""Choice D best synthesizes key findings by illustrating the promising outlook for renewable energy combined with the emergence of new battery technologies while cautioning that fossil fuel dependence persists in certain regions lacking robust infrastructure. Choices A, B, and C contain relevant points but do not offer the broader conclusion the student aims to highlight regarding the coexistence of ambitious technological advancements and continued reliance on traditional fuels. Choice A focuses more on growth projections, Choice B mainly stresses recycling, and Choice C focuses narrowly on one regional example."", ""topic"": ""The future of renewable energy and battery technology""}",Synthesizing Notes,Hard,"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes from the 2023 White Paper by the Global Energy Institute:

