• Replace the original opening clause with: ""Catherine the Great, along with her trusted advisors,"" 
  — This adjustment introduces a compound structure that tempts an incorrect plural verb choice.
• Keep the remainder of the sentence as is so that the context still indicates a completed historical action.
• The correct answer remains ""founded,"" since the singular primary subject requires a simple past to match both the subject-verb agreement and the historical context.

By incorporating this compound subject, the question now tests both the correct use of past tense and a nuanced understanding of subject-verb agreement in complex constructions—meeting the Hard difficulty criteria.

