2025-05-21 08:18:57,"{""skill"": ""Word Choice"", ""difficulty"": ""Medium"", ""question"": ""Ionizing radiation can generate free radicals that directly damage living cells, including DNA and proteins. Once formed, these highly reactive particles can  ________  crucial cellular structures, potentially resulting in mutations, cell death, or other forms of tissue harm when exposure is sufficiently high.\n\nWhich choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?"", ""choices"": [""A) disperse"", ""B) rectify"", ""C) prolong"", ""D) compromise""], ""answer"": ""D"", ""explanation"": ""Choice D is the best answer because in this context \""compromise\"" means to weaken or undermine the integrity of cellular components. The text indicates that once free radicals are formed, they have the potential to damage DNA and proteins, ultimately harming cells. Thus, \""compromise\"" accurately reflects how free radicals can reduce the stability and effectiveness of these crucial structures.\n\nChoices A, B, and C are incorrect. \""Disperse\"" suggests scattering or distributing, which does not convey the idea of harming intracellular molecules. \""Rectify\"" implies correcting or fixing and doesn’t match the damage caused by free radicals. \""Prolong\"" implies extending a duration, not weakening structures. Therefore, these choices do not fit the context of the sentence."", ""topic"": ""The effects of ionizing radiation on biological tissue""}",Word Choice,Medium,"Ionizing radiation can generate free radicals that directly damage living cells, including DNA and proteins. Once formed, these highly reactive particles can  ________  crucial cellular structures, potentially resulting in mutations, cell death, or other forms of tissue harm when exposure is sufficiently high.

