2025-05-21 08:31:53,"{""skill"": ""Word Choice"", ""difficulty"": ""Hard"", ""question"": ""Scientists studying the molecular basis of cancer have revealed how certain mutated genes spur malignant cells to proliferate rapidly. This discovery spurred the development of targeted therapies that exploit vulnerable segments of tumor-specific pathways without harming most healthy tissues. By specifically blocking the signals that drive continuous replication, these treatments can ________ cancer growth and minimize damage to surrounding cells.\n\nWhich choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?"", ""choices"": [""A. entrench"", ""B. curtail"", ""C. debunk"", ""D. buttress""], ""answer"": ""B"", ""explanation"": ""In this context, the best choice is “curtail,” which means to limit or reduce. The text discusses how targeted therapies aim to reduce, rather than reinforce or expose, cancer growth. “Entrench” means “to establish firmly,” which would suggest the treatments strengthen or secure cancer cell growth, an idea contrary to the intended outcome. “Debunk” means “to expose the falseness of,” which wouldn’t make sense when describing a treatment’s goal against cancer. “Buttress” means “to reinforce or support,” which similarly contradicts the goal of weakening cancer growth. Therefore, “curtail” logically fits the sentence and the overall idea that these targeted therapies reduce tumor proliferation."", ""topic"": ""The molecular basis of cancer and targeted therapies""}",Word Choice,Hard,"Scientists studying the molecular basis of cancer have revealed how certain mutated genes spur malignant cells to proliferate rapidly. This discovery spurred the development of targeted therapies that exploit vulnerable segments of tumor-specific pathways without harming most healthy tissues. By specifically blocking the signals that drive continuous replication, these treatments can ________ cancer growth and minimize damage to surrounding cells.

