2025-05-21 08:45:23,"{""skill"": ""Absolute Value"", ""difficulty"": ""Medium"", ""question"": ""Which of the following is the larger solution to the equation $\\lvert 3x - 4 \\rvert = x + 2$?\n\n"", ""choices"": [""A. 1"", ""B. 3"", ""C. -5"", ""D. 0.5""], ""answer"": ""B"", ""explanation"": ""To solve the equation $\\lvert 3x - 4 \\rvert = x + 2$, we consider two cases and then choose the larger valid solution.\n\nStep 1: Case 1: Solve $3x - 4 = x + 2$.\n\n3x - x = 2 + 4\n\n2x = 6\n\nx = 3\n\nStep 2: Case 2: Solve $3x - 4 = -(x + 2)$.\n\n3x - 4 = -x - 2\n\n3x + x = -2 + 4\n\n4x = 2\n\nx = 0.5\n\nStep 3: Check each solution in the original equation.\n\nBoth x = 3 and x = 0.5 satisfy $\\lvert 3x - 4 \\rvert = x + 2$. The problem asks for the larger solution, which is 3.\n\nTherefore, the larger solution is 3."", ""topic"": ""solving an absolute value equation with two solutions and choosing the larger value""}",Absolute Value,Medium,"Which of the following is the larger solution to the equation $\lvert 3x - 4 \rvert = x + 2$?

