2025-05-21 11:47:01,"{""skill"": ""Interpreting Graphs"", ""difficulty"": ""Medium"", ""question"": ""The table below shows the total number of website visitors for a business from January to June. Use the table to answer the question that follows.\n\n<table border='1'><thead><tr><th>Month</th><th>Number of visitors</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>January</td><td>6000</td></tr><tr><td>February</td><td>6400</td></tr><tr><td>March</td><td>7000</td></tr><tr><td>April</td><td>8000</td></tr><tr><td>May</td><td>8600</td></tr><tr><td>June</td><td>9000</td></tr></tbody></table>\n\nBased on the table, which of the following is closest to the average monthly increase in website visitors from January to June?\n\nA. 400\nB. 500\nC. 600\nD. 900"", ""choices"": [""A. 400"", ""B. 500"", ""C. 600"", ""D. 900""], ""answer"": ""C"", ""explanation"": ""To find the average monthly increase in visitors, we first find the difference in visitors between consecutive months, then sum those differences and divide by the number of intervals.\n\nStep 1: Calculate consecutive increases. February minus January = 6400 − 6000 = 400, March minus February = 7000 − 6400 = 600, April minus March = 8000 − 7000 = 1000, May minus April = 8600 − 8000 = 600, June minus May = 9000 − 8600 = 400.\n\nStep 2: Add these increases. 400 + 600 + 1000 + 600 + 400 = 3000.\n\nStep 3: There are 5 intervals in total, so we divide 3000 by 5, which yields 600.\n\nHence, the closest average monthly increase is 600."", ""topic"": ""Analyzing website visitor data""}",Interpreting Graphs,Medium,"The table below shows the total number of website visitors for a business from January to June. Use the table to answer the question that follows.

