2025-05-21 11:49:46,"{""skill"": ""Interpreting Graphs"", ""difficulty"": ""Hard"", ""question"": ""Company X and Company Y each reported net profits, in thousands of dollars, for the four quarters of 2019 and for the four quarters of 2020. The tables below show the data.\n\n<table border=\""1\"">\n<thead>\n<tr><th>Quarter</th><th>Net profit for Company X</th></tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td>2019 Q1</td><td>60</td></tr>\n<tr><td>2019 Q2</td><td>75</td></tr>\n<tr><td>2019 Q3</td><td>80</td></tr>\n<tr><td>2019 Q4</td><td>90</td></tr>\n<tr><td>2020 Q1</td><td>100</td></tr>\n<tr><td>2020 Q2</td><td>85</td></tr>\n<tr><td>2020 Q3</td><td>79</td></tr>\n<tr><td>2020 Q4</td><td>95</td></tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n\n<table border=\""1\"">\n<thead>\n<tr><th>Quarter</th><th>Net profit for Company Y</th></tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td>2019 Q1</td><td>55</td></tr>\n<tr><td>2019 Q2</td><td>70</td></tr>\n<tr><td>2019 Q3</td><td>85</td></tr>\n<tr><td>2019 Q4</td><td>85</td></tr>\n<tr><td>2020 Q1</td><td>89</td></tr>\n<tr><td>2020 Q2</td><td>93</td></tr>\n<tr><td>2020 Q3</td><td>80</td></tr>\n<tr><td>2020 Q4</td><td>100</td></tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n\nIf each company’s total net profit in a given year is the sum of its four quarterly net profits, which statement about the difference in total net profits from 2019 to 2020 for the two companies is correct?"", ""choices"": [""A. The difference in total net profits from 2019 to 2020 was 13 thousand dollars greater for Company Y than for Company X"", ""B. The difference in the sum of Company X’s net profits from 2019 to 2020 was 25 thousand dollars less than the difference in Company Y’s net profits for the same period"", ""C. The sum of Company X’s net profits from 2019 to 2020 increased by 70 thousand dollars, which is 22 thousand dollars more than the increase for Company Y"", ""D. The total net profit for both companies combined was 10 thousand dollars greater in 2019 than in 2020""], ""answer"": ""A"", ""explanation"": ""First, add Company X’s four quarterly net profits for 2019 (60 + 75 + 80 + 90 = 305) and for 2020 (100 + 85 + 79 + 95 = 359). The difference for Company X is 359 − 305 = 54. Next, add Company Y’s four quarterly net profits for 2019 (55 + 70 + 85 + 85 = 295) and for 2020 (89 + 93 + 80 + 100 = 362). The difference for Company Y is 362 − 295 = 67. Therefore, the difference for Company Y is 67 − 54 = 13 thousand dollars greater than that for Company X. A recommended strategy is to carefully compute each total and then compare year-over-year differences."", ""topic"": ""Interpreting Data from Tables""}",Interpreting Graphs,Hard,"Company X and Company Y each reported net profits, in thousands of dollars, for the four quarters of 2019 and for the four quarters of 2020. The tables below show the data.

