","{""skill"": ""Interpreting Graphs"", ""difficulty"": ""Hard"", ""question"": ""Company $X$ and Company $Y$ each reported net profits, in thousands of dollars, for the four quarters of $2019$ and for the four quarters of $2020$. The tables below show the data.\n\n\\[ \\begin{array}{|c|c|} \\hline \\text{Quarter} & \\text{Net profit for Company X (in thousands)} \\\\ \\hline \\text{2019 Q1} & 60 \\\\ \\text{2019 Q2} & 75 \\\\ \\text{2019 Q3} & 80 \\\\ \\text{2019 Q4} & 90 \\\\ \\text{2020 Q1} & 100 \\\\ \\text{2020 Q2} & 85 \\\\ \\text{2020 Q3} & 79 \\\\ \\text{2020 Q4} & 95 \\\\ \\hline \\end{array} \\]\n\n\\[ \\begin{array}{|c|c|} \\hline \\text{Quarter} & \\text{Net profit for Company Y (in thousands)} \\\\ \\hline \\text{2019 Q1} & 55 \\\\ \\text{2019 Q2} & 70 \\\\ \\text{2019 Q3} & 85 \\\\ \\text{2019 Q4} & 85 \\\\ \\text{2020 Q1} & 89 \\\\ \\text{2020 Q2} & 93 \\\\ \\text{2020 Q3} & 80 \\\\ \\text{2020 Q4} & 100 \\\\ \\hline \\end{array} \\]\n\nIf each company’s total net profit in a given year is the sum of its four quarterly net profits, which statement about the difference in total net profits from $2019$ to $2020$ for the two companies is correct?"", ""choices"": [""A. The difference in total net profits from $2019$ to $2020$ was $13$ thousand dollars greater for Company $Y$ than for Company $X$."", ""B. The difference in the sum of Company $X$’s net profits from $2019$ to $2020$ was $25$ thousand dollars less than the difference in Company $Y$’s net profits for the same period."", ""C. The sum of Company $X$’s net profits from $2019$ to $2020$ increased by $70$ thousand dollars, which is $22$ thousand dollars more than the increase for Company $Y$."", ""D. The total net profit for both companies combined was $10$ thousand dollars greater in $2019$ than in $2020$.""], ""answer"": ""A"", ""explanation"": ""First, compute the total net profits for Company $X$ in $2019$ and $2020$: \\[ \\text{For 2019: } 60 + 75 + 80 + 90 = 305 \\] \\[ \\text{For 2020: } 100 + 85 + 79 + 95 = 359 \\] \\[ \\text{Difference: } 359 - 305 = 54 \\]\n\nNext, compute the total net profits for Company $Y$ in $2019$ and $2020$: \\[ \\text{For 2019: } 55 + 70 + 85 + 85 = 295 \\] \\[ \\text{For 2020: } 89 + 93 + 80 + 100 = 362 \\] \\[ \\text{Difference: } 362 - 295 = 67 \\]\n\nFinally, compare the differences: \\[ 67 - 54 = 13 \\] The difference in total net profits from $2019$ to $2020$ for Company $Y$ is $13$ thousand dollars greater than that for Company $X$.\n\nNow, evaluate the other choices:\n- Choice $B$ is incorrect because the calculated difference is $13$ thousand dollars, not $25$ thousand dollars.\n- Choice $C$ is incorrect as it misstates the increases.\n- Choice $D$ is incorrect as the combined totals for $2019$ and $2020$ show an increase, not a decrease.\n\nThe correct answer is \\textbf{A}."", ""topic"": ""Interpreting Data from Tables""}","Company $X$ and Company $Y$ each reported net profits, in thousands of dollars, for the four quarters of $2019$ and for the four quarters of $2020$. The tables below show the data.

