• Content & Clarity: The question clearly presents two HTML tables embedded in the question, provides all necessary data (average temperatures, surcharge formulas, and the 30‐day month assumption), and asks a specific question about the difference between City X’s and City Y’s total surcharges. This meets guideline (1) and (2).

• Answer Choices: Four answer choices are provided with exactly one correct answer (Choice C) and three plausible distractors. This fully satisfies guideline (3).

• Explanation: The explanation outlines the step‐by‐step process—identifying when surcharges apply, computing each month’s total surcharge, and then summing totals—to arrive at the 162‑dollar difference. Although the core reasoning is clear, adding a brief note on why each distractor is incorrect would further enhance the educational value per guideline (4).

