  • Replace ""\\(S = 0.10(T - 50)\\)"" with ""$S = 0.10(T - 50)$"" 
  • Replace ""\\(T > 50\\)"" with ""$T > 50$""

This adjustment will meet guideline (5).

• Difficulty Level: Because the problem involves reading data from more than a single table while applying formulas and performing multi‐step arithmetic (and dealing with conditional surcharge calculations), it satisfies the expectations for a Hard difficulty question per guideline (6).

Overall, the question is high quality and nearly meets all standards. The only required improvement is to adjust the LaTeX formatting for math expressions (and optionally enrich the explanation by briefly discussing why the distractors are wrong).

