c{5}{2}x = 4. \\]\n\nSo\n\n\\[ x = \\frac{8}{5}. \\]\n\nSubstituting back,\n\n\\[ y = 2(\\frac{8}{5}) - 11 = \\frac{16}{5} - 11 = -\\frac{39}{5}. \\]\n\nHence, $(p,q) = \\left( \\frac{8}{5}, -\\frac{39}{5} \\right)$.\n\nThe value $p - m$ is\n\n\\[ \\frac{8}{5} - \\left( -\\frac{8}{5} \\right) = \\frac{16}{5}. \\]\n\nSo choice C is correct."", ""topic"": ""Lines with parallel and perpendicular slopes""}","Consider the lines $L_1$ and $L_2$ in the xy-plane, both of which have slope $2$. Suppose $L_1$ passes through $(2,1)$ and $L_2$ passes through $(4,-3)$. Another line, $L_3$, is perpendicular to them and passes through the midpoint of the y-intercepts of $L_1$ and $L_2$.

