B) 4
C) 6
D) 8",C,"First, solve for y in line k to get $\y = 6 - 2x\$. Next, find the intersection Q by setting $\6 - 2x\$ equal to $\x - 5\$. Solving $\6 - 2x = x - 5\$ gives $\6 + 5 = x + 2x\$, or $\11 = 3x\$, so $\x = \frac{11}{3}\$. Substituting into $\y = x - 5\$ yields $\y = \frac{11}{3} - 5 = -\frac{4}{3}\$. Thus Q is $\left(\frac{11}{3}, -\frac{4}{3}\right)\$.

