","{""skill"": ""Linear Word Problems"", ""difficulty"": ""Easy"", ""question"": ""One weekend, a community center pays a band a fixed fee of $200 plus $5 for every ticket sold. \\[ \\text{If the total amount paid to the band was $500, how many tickets were sold?} \\]"", ""choices"": [""A. 40"", ""B. 60"", ""C. 65"", ""D. 100""], ""answer"": ""B"", ""explanation"": ""The problem asks for the number of tickets sold such that the total payment to the band equals $500.\\\n\\\n\\( \\text{Step 1: Define the variable. Let } x \\text{ be the number of tickets sold. The total payment is given as } 200 + 5x. \\)\\\n\\\n\\( \\text{Step 2: Set up an equation representing the total payment.}\\)\\\n\\(200 + 5x = 500\\)\\\n\\\n\\( \\text{Step 3: Solve for } x: \\)\\\n\\(200 + 5x = 500\\)\\\n\\(5x = 500 - 200\\)\\\n\\(5x = 300\\)\\\n\\(x = \\frac{300}{5}\\)\\\n\\(x = 60\\)\\\n\\\nThus, 60 tickets were sold.\\\n\\\n\\( \\text{Additional explanation: Validate other choices. Option A (40 tickets) would yield } 200 + 5(40) = 400, \\text{ so it is too low. Option C (65 tickets) results in } 200 + 5(65) = 525, \\text{ so it is too high. Option D (100 tickets) produces } 200 + 5(100) = 700, \\text{ which is also too high. Therefore, only Option B (60 tickets) satisfies the condition.}\\)"", ""topic"": ""Costs and Tickets""}","One weekend, a community center pays a band a fixed fee of $200 plus $5 for every ticket sold. \[ \text{If the total amount paid to the band was $500, how many tickets were sold?} \]","A. 40
