2025-05-21 13:21:36,"{""skill"": ""Inequality Word Problems"", ""difficulty"": ""Medium"", ""question"": ""Mina is organizing a school event. She must pay a $110 facility fee plus $9 per table. She wants to keep her total cost at or below $350.\n\nWhich of the following is the maximum integer value of x, the number of tables, that satisfies the inequality?"", ""choices"": [""A. 26"", ""B. 27"", ""C. 28"", ""D. 29""], ""answer"": ""A"", ""explanation"": ""The total cost is given by $110 + 9x$. For the cost to be at or below 350, set up the inequality $110 + 9x \\leq 350$.\n\nStep 1: Subtract 110 from both sides:\n$9x \\leq 240$.\n\nStep 2: Divide both sides by 9:\n$x \\leq \\frac{240}{9} = 26.\\overline{6}.$\n\nStep 3: Since x must be an integer, the maximum integer not exceeding 26.\\overline{6} is 26. Therefore, choice A is correct."", ""topic"": ""School event table rentals""}",Inequality Word Problems,Medium,"Mina is organizing a school event. She must pay a $110 facility fee plus $9 per table. She wants to keep her total cost at or below $350.

Which of the following is the maximum integer value of x, the number of tables, that satisfies the inequality?","A. 26
B. 27
C. 28
D. 29",A,"The total cost is given by $110 + 9x$. For the cost to be at or below 350, set up the inequality $110 + 9x \leq 350$.

