These revisions will further enhance clarity and adherence to the highest professional standards.","{""skill"": ""Systems of Equations"", ""difficulty"": ""Hard"", ""question"": ""Luisa is designing a rectangular model for a future courtyard. The length of the rectangle is \\( x \\) feet, and the width is \\( y \\) feet. The system of equations below describes the perimeter and a relationship involving the modified rectangle's area:\n\n\\[\n2x + 2y = 66\n\\]\n\n\\[\nxy - (x + 5)(y - 2) = 14\n\\]\n\nWhich of the following is the value of \\( x \\)?"", ""choices"": [""A. \\( \\frac{169}{7} \\)"", ""B. 25"", ""C. \\( \\frac{137}{7} \\)"", ""D. \\( \\frac{156}{7} \\)""], ""answer"": ""A"", ""explanation"": ""To solve for \\( x \\), begin with the perimeter equation:\n\n\\[ x + y = 33. \\]\n\nNext, expand and simplify the modified area equation:\n\n\\[\nxy - (xy - 2x + 5y - 10) = 14,\n\\]\n\nwhich reduces to:\n\n\\[\n2x - 5y + 10 = 14,\n\\]\n\nor:\n\n\\[\n2x - 5y = 4.\\]\n\nSubstituting \\( y = 33 - x \\) into \\( 2x - 5y = 4 \\) gives:\n\n\\[\n2x - 5(33 - x) = 4.\n\\]\n\nSimplifying:\n\n\\[\n2x - 165 + 5x = 4,\n\\]\n\nor:\n\n\\[\n7x - 165 = 4.\n\\]\n\nSolving for \\( x \\):\n\n\\[\nx = \\frac{169}{7}.\\]\n\nThus, the correct answer is \\( \\frac{169}{7} \\), and choice A is correct.\n\nTo confirm, substituting \\( x = \\frac{169}{7} \\) and \\( y = 33 - x \\) into both equations shows they hold true. Substituting any other value for \\( x \\) results in a \\( y \\) that does not satisfy both equations, eliminating the other choices."", ""topic"": ""Harder linear system word problem""}","Luisa is designing a rectangular model for a future courtyard. The length of the rectangle is \( x \) feet, and the width is \( y \) feet. The system of equations below describes the perimeter and a relationship involving the modified rectangle's area:

