2025-05-21 15:06:24,"{""skill"": ""Unit Conversions"", ""difficulty"": ""Medium"", ""question"": ""A landscaper needs 2.5 cubic yards of concrete mix for a small patio project.\n\nEach bag of a certain concrete mix produces 2 cubic feet of concrete when prepared according to the manufacturer’s instructions. If 1 yard = 3 feet, how many bags of this concrete mix are required?"", ""choices"": [""A. 28"", ""B. 34"", ""C. 67"", ""D. 84""], ""answer"": ""B"", ""explanation"": ""First, convert 2.5 cubic yards to cubic feet. One yard equals 3 feet, so one cubic yard equals 3 × 3 × 3, or 27, cubic feet.\n\nStep 1: Multiply 2.5 cubic yards by 27 to find the total volume in cubic feet:\n\n2.5 × 27 = 67.5 cubic feet.\n\nStep 2: Each bag of the concrete mix yields 2 cubic feet, so divide the total cubic feet by 2 to find the number of bags needed:\n\n67.5 ÷ 2 = 33.75.\n\nStep 3: Since 33.75 is not a whole number of bags, the landscaper must use the next whole number of bags:\n\n33.75 rounds up to 34 bags.\n\nTherefore, 34 bags are required."", ""topic"": ""Concrete Volume Conversion""}",Unit Conversions,Medium,"A landscaper needs 2.5 cubic yards of concrete mix for a small patio project.

